In article <2433@wheaton.UUCP> kroth@wheaton.UUCP (Ken Roth) writes:
>You can also use a
>help of opposite alignment, and sacrifice at any altar you want, just keep
>re-wearing the helm until you are the correct alignment.

First of all, that's a *helm* of opposite alignment, not a help.  Second,
make sure the helm is uncursed - you'll have to do this yourself, as all
helms of opposite alignment are automatically cursed.  Third, I'm pretty 
sure that this won't work quite the way you describe it unless you are of
neutral alignment.  You see, if you're chaotic or lawful, it will truly
change you to the *opposite* alignment, so you'd never be able to be neutral
with the helm.  However, if you start neutral, it will randomly pick either
chaotic or lawful for you each time you wear it.

